  "summary": "A 41,332-tumour analysis dates whole-genome doubling relative to drivers, losses and immune programmes, alongside somatic mosaicism and variant-calling advances.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the evolutionary timing of whole-genome doubling (WGD) in human cancer. A pan-cancer analysis of 41,332 tumours across 12 cancer types dates WGD relative to driver events, chromosomal losses and immune programmes. A related preprint maps mosaic chromosomal alterations across 19 tissues from 722 WGS samples, reporting tissue-specific mitotic error and purifying selection; it concerns non-tumour tissue and is not doubling-specific. The remaining items are methodological and peripheral: pangenome-based somatic variant calling, somatic retrotransposition mapping, PDX mouse-content estimation, and plant somatic mutation and epigenetic assays. They do not address WGD directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
